            <ArticleTitle>[Evolution of coronary occlusion in a patient with past myocardial infarction (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>997-1000</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a man suffering from an anterior myocardial infarction with complete occlusion of the left descendent coronary angiographically proved is reported: an angiographic control four months after aorto-coronary by-pass on right coronary, showed the recanalization of left anterior descendent coronary and occlusion of the by-pass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
